## Usage

```bash
# Initialize and select dev stack
pulumi stack init dev
pulumi config set environment dev
pulumi config set dbInstanceClass db.t3.micro
pulumi config set dbMultiAz false
pulumi config set dbAllocatedStorage 20
pulumi config set enableReplication false
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword "$(openssl rand -base64 32)"

# Deploy dev
pulumi up

# Initialize and select prod stack
pulumi stack init prod
pulumi config set environment prod
pulumi config set dbInstanceClass db.t3.medium
pulumi config set dbMultiAz true
pulumi config set dbAllocatedStorage 100
pulumi config set enableReplication true
pulumi config set replicationRegion us-west-2
pulumi config set --secret dbPassword "$(openssl rand -base64 32)"

# Deploy prod (independent state, no impact on dev)
pulumi up
```

## Acceptance Criteria Mapping

| Criterion | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Bucket**: versioning, encryption, no public access | `BucketVersioningV2` enabled, `AES256` SSE, `BucketPublicAccessBlock` all four flags `true` |
| **RDS**: deletion protection, backup ≥7d, not public | `deletionProtection: true`, `backupRetentionPeriod: 14`, `publiclyAccessible: false` |
| **Secret**: never plaintext in Git | `config.requireSecret()` → Pulumi `ConfigSecret`, encrypted in stack file; stored in Secrets Manager |
| **IAM**: least privilege, no wildcards on prod | Policy scoped to specific bucket ARN and secret ARN; prod uses OIDC trust with `StringEquals` on service account subject |
| **Environment isolation** | Separate Pulumi stacks (`dev`, `prod`) with independent state files and config; `pulumi up` on one stack never touches the other |
